            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>A knitted component for an article of footwear includes a knit element defining an upper and a gusseted tongue formed of unitary knit construction with the knit element and extending through a portion of an instep area of the upper. The upper includes an exterior surface and an opposite interior surface. A portion of the knit element overlaps a lateral side edge and a medial side edge of the gusseted tongue along opposite sides of the instep area. The lateral side edge and the medial side edge remain unsecured to the knit element. The gusseted tongue is joined to the knit element at a forward portion of the instep area. The lateral side edge and the medial side edge of the gusseted tongue are secured to the knit element along the forward portion of the instep area so as to form the knitted component as a one-piece element.</p>
            </abstract>
